WEBVTT

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.600
Play!

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.360
Strike!

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:14.990
<i>Every time I catch one of his pitches, it feels like I receive some amazing energy from him.{AMS: ep4 22:34}</i>

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.700
<i>And... beyond his energy, I can feel it!{AMS: ep4 22:44}</i>

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:21.620
It got through!{AMS: ep4 22:56}

00:01:58.760 --> 00:01:59.970
All right!

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:05.850
Go, Shimizu!

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.230
Run for home!

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:22.040
S-Safe!

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:25.240
All right! We caught up!

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.950
All right!

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:30.350
Nice running, Kaoru-chan!

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.750
Nice, softball girl!

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.800
How pathetic!

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.230
You said you would win by yourself!

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:44.010
You ended up having to rely on a girl and an amateur to tie the score.

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:51.190
At this point, the whole thing about you winning by yourself is void.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:53.160
What are you talking about?

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:57.180
At least two runs were scored because of your horrible play!

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.190
Shut up! A bet's a bet!

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:03.660
Even if you win, you're cheating, so I won't join this team!

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:11.290
Excuse me, Seishuu? Who's the next batter?

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:15.510
H-Hey, Tashiro, that's you, right?

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:22.290
Tashiro!

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:24.810
I got it.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:27.680
If you're going to take it this far, I won't force you anymore.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:33.810
Not just Tashiro... everyone else, too. If you don't want to there's nothing I can do about it.

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:41.240
Of course it'll be a problem for me, but there's always a possibility of gathering members from the first-years coming in next year.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:46.210
Then... why did you start such a reckless gamble, Nogoro-kun?

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:52.800
If you knew anything about baseball, you should've known that it wouldn't be easy to win a game by yourself.

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:57.430
I guess I'm just stupid.

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:01.840
I seriously thought that if I gave everyone a bat and a glove,

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.030
and pulled them out under the blue sky,

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:07.510
they'd definitely fall in love with baseball.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:16.460
But, when I think about it,

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:20.360
there's no way a game where you just stand still can be fun at all.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:24.100
I was the only one that was having fun.

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:28.490
Play!

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.210
Strike!

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:43.760
Ball!

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:48.050
<i>What's up with this guy? It's dangerous...</i>

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.850
<i>Isn't he watching the ball at all?</i>

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:52.770
<i>Why?</i>

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:56.270
<i>Why did that baseball idiot come to our school?</i>

00:04:58.810 --> 00:04:59.730
Strike!

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:04.280
<i>Quit fooling around... It's just annoying for me now!</i>

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:06.780
<i>What? Seishuu?</i>

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.430
<i>Yes.</i>

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:11.950
<i>Up until now I've let you play baseball to build character,</i>

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:16.460
<i>but I want you to start studying harder now.</i>

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.230
<i>W-Why?</i>

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:21.260
<i>I was going to try and become a pro and take the test to get into Kaido!</i>

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:25.380
<i>Stop chasing a dream that has such a small chance of actually happening!</i>

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:29.090
<i>You have a responsibility to take over my business after me.</i>

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:34.570
<i>You no longer have any need for baseball in your life!</i>

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.470
Strike! Batter out!

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.650
Three outs! Change!

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.610
<i>That's right...</i>

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:44.550
<i>I threw baseball away two years ago.</i>

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:46.950
<i>A baseball team here and now...</i>

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.580
Strike! Batter out!

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.330
Change!

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:04.460
Hey, Tashiro...

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:07.340
Isn't this enough?

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:09.770
Shigeno is trying so hard,

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:12.210
and he says that all we have to do is stand there during games.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.090
Let's just join...

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:16.190
If you want to do it, just do it!

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.730
Stop joking around!

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:20.150
How could you guys possibly understand my feelings?

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:29.360
W-What's going on? What's wrong?

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.320
Fuji was...

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:33.540
Something seemed wrong so we took off his glove and...

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.200
W-What's up with your hand?

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:39.290
Looks like it hurts!

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:40.940
This isn't good...

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.670
It seems like it's swelling caused by a broken bone.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:49.220
Probably because he was catching Nogoro-kun's pitches.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.330
I-Idiot!

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:53.950
If it hurts then hurry up and say so!

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:56.170
Why would you wait until it got this bad?

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:57.560
How could I... say anything?

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.180
How could I... say anything?

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:02.120
If I made you worry about my hand...

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:05.370
then you wouldn't be able to throw with all your might.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:09.370
Besides, there's no one other than me to play catcher!

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:12.580
If I said anything, the game would be cancelled.

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:20.930
What would happen if an amateur tried so hard in an exhibition game?

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:23.750
That's... what I want to know!

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:26.610
Up until now,

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:29.460
I've always ran away from things that seemed too bothersome.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.810
It started with my childhood activities.

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:34.990
In elementary and middle school,

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:37.640
I joined a few clubs, but quit after only three days.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:40.180
The same with the Little League baseball that I used to play.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.290
But, you know what?

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.360
This time... something's different.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.220
I get the feeling that if I don't do my best now,

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:51.740
I'll never find anything else ever again!

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:59.560
That's why this pain in my hand is nothing!

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.790
It might just be an amateur's exhibition game,

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:05.320
but I don't want to do things half-heartedly anymore!

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.050
Strike! Batter out!

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.300
Three outs! Change!

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:20.870
It's all right. I completely understand your feelings.

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:25.400
But I can't continue to pitch to someone with that kind of injury.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:27.810
S-Shigeno...

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.930
Let's just quit here.

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:33.070
Even if this game ends here,

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:37.220
no one here will think that you do things half-heartedly.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:53.880
I understand.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:57.040
Then... I'll go and talk to them.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:58.850
Wait just a minute.

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:03.310
I'll catch for you.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:04.280
Huh?

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:04.280
What?

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:07.220
You bastard, what are you thinking?

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:10.480
I'm not planning anything.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.480
It's just that...

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:15.950
watching you made me want to stop being half-hearted as well.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.700
Can you catch them?

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.910
If you can't then it'll just be bothersome.

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:25.500
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:30.760
I won't let you off easily if you hold back against a guy who played catcher the entire time he played in the Little and Senior Leagues.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:31.710
Wha-

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.800
What!?

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:39.090
Play!

00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:44.370
<i>That bastard... is he serious?</i>

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:45.980
<i>Former catcher?</i>

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.570
Strike!

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:54.690
H-He caught it?

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:57.030
No... didn't it just go in?

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:03.950
<i>This feeling... it's so nostalgic.</i>

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.230
You can actually do it.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:16.450
Ball!

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:18.630
<i>He's catching them!</i>

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:20.960
<i>This guy... he's actually watching my pitches and catching them!</i>

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:25.060
<i>This guy... he's actually watching my pitches and catching them!</i>

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:29.100
<i>I'm sorry... Dad.</i>

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:33.520
Strike!

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:35.070
<i>But...</i>

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:40.950
<i>you believe that there are dreams in this world that you run after and regret,</i>

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.910
<i>but in this'</i> world I don't believe that!

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.910
<i>but in </i>this world I don't believe that!

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:46.920
<i>Not me!</i>

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.620
Strike! Batter out!

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:51.360
Yeah!

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:59.260
<i>Looks like the catcher's position was stolen from me.</i>

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:01.350
This is our last at-bat!

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:03.470
We can't lose, can we?

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:17.480
Yeah! It's a walk-off home run!

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:17.480
{ - Clatter - (TL)}{AMS: TLC couldn't hear this}{sangofe: I believe it's only sounds -sangofe}

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:17.500
Yeah! We did it!{I don't think this is said, so comment it out? -sangofe}

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:19.050
{- Missing Translation -}{AMS: TLC couldn't hear this}{yeah, let's cut this out -sangofe}{that was a nice duel?}

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:20.200
Great job! {Added by timer, TLC}

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:20.200
Yeah!

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:24.660
So you ended up grabbing the great parts for yourself...

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:24.650
{ - clatter - (TL)}{AMS: TLC couldn't hear this}

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:29.170
We did it! Shigeno! That was amazing!

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:30.450
I see...

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:33.430
For some reason,

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:36.400
I feel like defeating Kaido with him too.

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:42.850
This is a free fansub.

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:42.850
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:45.140
It'll take a month to heal!?

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:46.850
Yeah.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:49.600
I'm lucky that this is all that happened.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:53.100
To tell you the truth, I thought it'd be worse than just a cracked bone.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.210
It's because you overdid it...

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:57.520
Well, take your time and heal up.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:01.510
The other dependable half of the battery has shown up!

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:05.890
Yo! Tashiro!

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:09.240
You're coming out to practice starting today, right?

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:10.560
Practice?

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:13.210
Even if you ask me to come, where am I supposed to go?

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:15.430
Is there a clubhouse?

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:18.670
Do you have a field for us to use?

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:22.880
And also, you told the others they 
wouldn't need to come out to practice.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:26.300
With those conditions, how are you proposing we practice?

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:35.890
We can't get a field?

00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:37.520
According to the principal,

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:43.320
all the fields are currently crowded, and for the new baseball team that uses dangerous hard balls...

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:45.850
there are no fields for us to use.

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:49.340
Then where are you suggesting we practice?

00:12:49.340 --> 00:12:50.360
Yes...

00:12:50.840 --> 00:12:52.930
Well, as your advisor,

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:54.710
I did a lot of negotiating,

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:58.930
and the result of it was I received permission to use this rooftop as the practice area for the baseball team.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:00.420
What!?

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:00.420
What!?

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:04.090
Hey, this is concrete! Concrete!

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:06.890
We're going to get hurt if we practice up here!

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:08.030
Yes.

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:12.720
That's why I got permission to do one more thing.

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:15.180
Please, look at that.

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:21.190
The back of that mountain is school property...

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:23.900
The dirt there seems to be free.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:33.370
H-Hey... don't tell me... from there?

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:34.410
Yup!

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:37.510
Using the dirt from down there,

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:40.420
we'll bring it up to the roof and make a baseball field.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:52.910
Going through all that trouble to make a field up here,

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:54.630
where's the need for that?

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:56.090
If I'm going to have that much time,

00:13:56.090 --> 00:14:01.410
then it'd be better just to go someplace nearby and throw Tashiro some curve balls.

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:04.070
What about everyone else's practice?

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:05.570
"Everyone else's practice"?

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:10.130
You know that they're ghost members.

00:14:10.130 --> 00:14:13.360
There's no way they'd practice.

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:17.530
Are you really fine with that?

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:20.160
Nogoro-kun,

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:24.460
do you seriously believe that you will win against Kaido like that?

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:26.010
What?

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:36.900
I'll leave the rest for you to decide, Nogoro-kun.

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:45.530
But the school won't approve of a team that doesn't carry out proper training on proper grounds.

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:51.850
Unless you do as I say, and build a field up here on this rooftop,

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:58.650
plans to turn this club into an official team will be put on hold until training conditions are approved of.

00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:02.170
Hey, hey.

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:05.160
Are you seriously going to do it?

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:06.200
Well, what else can I do?

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:08.880
If we don't do it, he's saying he won't approve us as a team.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.970
You can go home you know.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:13.970
With that hand you'll just slow me down.

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:23.100
Guess I'll have to start with taking out the weeds.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.230
Hey, Shigeno,

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:27.650
shouldn't you tell the other guys from practice?

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:29.320
I'm fine by myself.

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:34.150
Besides, with it getting cold soon, it'll be like training for me.

00:15:34.150 --> 00:15:36.450
For me, this is just along the way.

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:40.330
What?

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:42.840
Shigeno is building a field by himself?

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:46.500
Yeah, he's been passionately doing so since yesterday.

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:49.940
If it's okay with you guys, why don't we help him a bit?

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:52.530
You're kidding, right?

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:55.700
We're ghost members that don't need to go to practice.

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:58.380
Why would we have to do something like that?

00:15:58.380 --> 00:16:00.750
That contradicts our agreement.

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:02.680
I refuse, I refuse.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:03.680
Right?

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:06.030
Uh... Y-Yeah...

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.070
Hey! What is up with this, sensei?

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:14.570
Why are you purposely getting him to do such a difficult task?

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:17.790
The school should provide a field for us!

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:18.610
Why now-

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:19.870
Shut up!

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:22.070
Stop talking.

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:26.580
This is one of the processes for Seishuu to get to Koshien.

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:28.100
K-Koshien?

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:29.550
K-Koshien?

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:50.860
H-Hey! Wait a second!

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:52.340
Honda!

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:54.450
What are you doing so early in the morning?

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:58.160
I'm making an amusement park on the roof.

00:16:58.570 --> 00:16:59.870
Huh?

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:07.300
Man! I've been bringing it up here since early in the morning, but there's still only this much.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:12.800
I have to dig out more dirt from there, too.

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:13.860
At this rate,

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:18.510
if I do something wrong, I might not be able to finish by the time the first-years arrive next year.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:27.520
Y-You guys!

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:31.980
How rude... How come you didn't say anything to us?

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:35.820
I'm the one that started the baseball team.

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:40.360
I don't want to bother anyone anymore.

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:45.470
Hey! Are you saying that for real?

00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:49.970
No one joined the baseball team for you!

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:51.610
I...

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:54.050
I started baseball for myself!

00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:00.340
Leave him alone.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:06.020
That guy doesn't understand normal people's feelings.

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:07.140
Tashiro...

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:08.730
But you know what?

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:14.190
I don't want to practice on a field that was built solely by Shigeno-sama!

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:16.530
Our field...

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.400
We can only build it ourselves, right?

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:22.600
That's right.

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:23.330
Yup, that's right.

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:44.140
{- Clatter - (TL)}{AMS: TLC couldn't hear}

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:48.150
Our senpai are working so hard... Is it okay?

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:51.380
But, we're ghost members...

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:55.850
But that last game... I got so excited!

00:18:55.850 --> 00:18:56.660
Yeah,

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:58.830
my heart was beating really fast!

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:00.140
Same here.

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:09.910
Man!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.840
This is heavy work for so early in the morning!

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:18.520
What? You're going to quit after saying something so cool?

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:20.180
I guess you really are useless.

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:22.440
What'd you say!?

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:22.440
Excuse me?

00:19:23.770 --> 00:19:25.600
What do you guys want?

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:28.590
We were talking with each other...

00:19:28.590 --> 00:19:31.060
And thought that we should help.

00:19:33.430 --> 00:19:36.860
After all, we are... part of the baseball team.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:42.320
Well then, I'm counting in you.

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:27.320
I wonder if it's really... all right if we don't help.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:31.000
Who cares? They're doing it because they want to.

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.190
Let's just leave them alone.

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:35.980
Tashiro's there... and the first-years are helping too.

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:38.100
I don't care about that.

00:20:38.820 --> 00:20:41.670
I'm going to go help them!

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:49.390
Do whatever you want! 

00:20:54.540 --> 00:21:00.650
When "m" equals one, "y" equals eight. {TL: I couldn't hear the  end......}

00:21:01.100 --> 00:21:06.120
{- Missing Translation -}{AMS: TLC can't hear}

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:09.690
{- Missing Translation -}{AMS: TLC can't hear}

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:27.460
Try your hardest, Uchiyama. We're almost there.

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:28.370
Yeah.

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:46.310
This is bothersome.

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:50.470
I couldn't stand just watching and doing nothing...

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:51.990
Hurry up and get this over with.

00:22:56.610 --> 00:22:58.810
I thought it would take longer...

00:22:59.740 --> 00:23:03.280
but these kids seem to have more will than I thought.

00:23:03.910 --> 00:23:08.990
I guess we should move onto phase two.

00:24:40.570 --> 00:24:43.330
Seishuu High School's baseball team has finally started to come together.

00:24:43.330 --> 00:24:46.910
And then as a Spartan coach, the person who volunteers is-

00:24:46.910 --> 00:24:48.210
What? Dad!?

00:24:48.670 --> 00:24:49.900
I didn't hear about this!

00:24:49.900 --> 00:24:51.960
Everyone... are you quitting baseball?

00:24:52.470 --> 00:24:53.770
Next time, on Major:

00:24:53.770 --> 00:24:55.010
Each One's Decision.

00:24:55.010 --> 00:24:57.570
Run to the stage of your dreams!
